  "body": "## What changed\n\nA new lathe Facing, whether created by MCP `add_operation` (`operation::seed_params`) or the GUI quick-add (`quick_params`), took its heights from the mill fold. That gave `top_z` = Top of Model and the facing plane `bottom_z` = Bottom of Model (the #214 floor). `turning::facing` then laddered from z 0 up to the part's top: it cut the part away and never touched the allowance above it.\n\n- `crates/app/src/operation/kinds.rs` `seed_facing`: the seed now states its own heights, the same way it already overrides the stepdown. `top_z` = Top of Stock + 0, and `bottom_z` (the facing plane) = Top of Model + 0. Both new-op paths retype the same Face draft, so both get these heights. Retyping an existing op into a Facing gets them too.\n- `crates/app/src/operation/heights_sel.rs` `depth_sane`: a part already at length (stock top == part top) makes the window level. The heights door used to refuse this as \"must cut downward: its top height resolves below its bottom height\", which is wrong for a level window. A Facing now passes a level window, as Face already does. `generate` then refuses by name: `nothing to face - the facing plane stands at or above the top of both the part and its stock`. This is the generator's existing `GenError::Empty`, so no new status was needed. A top below the plane is still refused by the door.\n- `docs/decisions/1409-face-seed-heights.md` records the decision.\n\nThe verify wording note from the issue is not changed. The 0.8 mm saturation of `gouge_mm` is shared by every envelope kind, so rewording it is not a trivial change. Verify semantics are untouched.\n\n## Pins (each mutation-checked)\n\nNew suite `crates/app/tests/turning_face_seed.rs` runs the issue's repro over the MCP server: `lathe.mch`, an r 10 × 48 bar as STL, 20 × 50 cylinder stock, `TN-1600-0R8`, then `add_operation` facing.\n\n| Pin | Mutation | Result |\n|---|---|---|\n| `a_seeded_facing_faces_the_allowance_not_the_part`: generate gives `ok`; verify gives `findings == []` and `ok`; fanuc-lathe posts the passes `G01 X-1.6` at exactly Z50, 49.5, 49, 48.5, 48 | seed back to `c.top` / `c.bottom` | red: verify findings not empty (the issue's gouge and rapid-in-stock) |\n| `the_facing_seed_runs_from_the_stock_top_to_the_part_top` (`seed_params`) | same | red |\n| `ui::egui_app::fresh_op_tests::a_quick_add_facing_runs_from_the_stock_top_to_the_part_top` (`quick_params`, and asserts it equals `seed_params`) | same | red |\n| `turning::the_facing_seed_faces_the_bar`: reworked to go through the real `seed_params` instead of a hand-built `Carried` with fixed 16/14 heights; asserts stepdown 0.5 and that no CL point sinks below the part top's tangency | same | red |\n| `a_seeded_facing_on_a_part_at_length_reports_nothing_to_face` (50 → 48 stock): generate errs with \"nothing to face\" | remove the Facing arm in `depth_sane` | red: `add_operation` refused (\"must cut downward\") |\n\nAfter each mutation the code was restored and every pin was green again.\n\n## Gates\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` on head 58be8266: green. App: lib, heights_selection, plasma_profile, probe_op, probe_search, ribbon, shoulder_adaptive, sinker_burn, sinker_side, tool_law, trochoid_op, turning, turning_face_seed, wire_contour. UI: lib, boundary, boundary_picks, theme_files.\n- Extra turning, post and MCP suites, all green: lathe_field_sim, lathe_post, lathe_post_css, lathe_post_g76, lathe_post_inch, lathe_post_tormach, lathe_post_tormach_thread, lathe_workholding_kinds, lathe_workholding_mill_post, tormach_lathes, turning_face_approach, turning_stock_approach, sim_lathe_body, setup_mounts_post, post_serves_kind, project_roundtrip, tool_cutting_rows, mcp_cutting, mcp_pick, mcp_verify. These include the fanuc_lathe_inch goldens (lathe_post_inch) and the Tormach lathe goldens.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean. camcraft-motion is untouched.\n\n## Goldens\n\nNo golden CL/NC files changed. The lathe golden and post suites build their Facing params explicitly, so they do not go through the seed. No snapshot PNGs touched.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The GUI quick-add was not clicked in the running app. It is pinned at `quick_params`, which is the function the ribbon action calls.\n- No hand test in PathPilot Hub.\n\nChangelog: A new lathe Facing (MCP add_operation or the ribbon quick-add) faces the stock allowance from Top of Stock down to Top of Model instead of cutting the part away from its bottom; a part already at length reports \"nothing to face\".\n\nEffort: high (no escalation). Fork synced at upstream/main 936172d8.\n\nFixes #1409\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n",
